From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 05:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a <webview>'s file chooser and downloads ask the
 shell

An `<input type="file">` in a browser window did nothing, and a download had
nowhere to ask where it goes. Both are a file picker, and a picker is desktop
UI: Chrome's answer is a dialog through the desktop portal, a GTK window the
shell did not draw. So the guest asks the element over WebViewGuestClient and
the shell draws the picker -- see `WebViewGuest::RunFileChooser` and
`WebViewGuest::ChooseDownloadPath` in `src/`.

What this patch carries is the part in files Chromium owns:

- `ChromeDownloadManagerDelegate::ShowFilePickerWithUserTakeover` hands a
  download from a guest to `WebViewGuest::ChooseDownloadPath` instead of
  `DownloadFilePicker`, and `download/BUILD.gn` depends on the target for it.
  It does so before Chrome's queue, which shows one picker at a time per
  profile: each window shows its own, so a picker nobody answers (a hidden
  window's) does not hold every later download.
- `PostProfileInit` turns on `download.prompt_for_download`, so every download
  asks. A download saved where nobody chose is a file the user never sees
  arrive: this desktop has no download shelf.
- The three Blink lists that build `DomicileFileChooserEvent`, beside
  patch 0035's `DomicileNewWindowEvent`.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the guards that
measure it -- `guard-webview-upload.sh` and `guard-webview-download.sh` -- run
on `crux` with the rest of the engine job.
---
 chrome/browser/chrome_browser_main.cc         |  4 +++
 chrome/browser/download/BUILD.gn              |  1 +
 .../chrome_download_manager_delegate.cc       | 30 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../renderer/bindings/generated_in_core.gni   |  2 ++
 .../blink/renderer/bindings/idl_in_core.gni   |  1 +
 .../blink/renderer/core/html/build.gni        |  2 ++
 6 files changed, 40 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_main.cc b/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_main.cc
index 3922e79..eaeae25 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_main.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_main.cc
@@ -1639,6 +1639,10 @@ void ChromeBrowserMainParts::PostProfileInit(Profile* profile,
   // drawn over the desktop. Before any window, so the shell's first page
   // already has none.
   domicile::TurnOffBrowserOffers(*profile->GetPrefs());
+  // And every download asks where it goes: the shell draws the picker, and a
+  // download saved to a folder nobody chose is a file the user never sees
+  // arrive -- this desktop has no download shelf to show it on.
+  profile->GetPrefs()->SetBoolean(prefs::kPromptForDownload, true);
 
   for (auto& chrome_extra_part : chrome_extra_parts_) {
     chrome_extra_part->PostProfileInit(profile, is_initial_profile);
